/-!
# The first reduction of the converse of Stacks 0GV1: to a finite morphism of finite presentation

Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space with the data of Stacks 0GUY: an
affine surjective étale chart `φ : V ⟶ X` factored as an open immersion `j : V ⟶ Y` and a finite
morphism `π : Y ⟶ X`, and a finite type quasi-coherent ideal `ℐ ⊆ 𝒪_Y` with
`V(ℐ) = Y ∖ j(V)`.  The first paragraph of the source's proof of the converse of Stacks 0GV1
shows that, if `π_*ℐ` is a quotient of a finite locally free module `ℰ`, the same holds for data
of this kind in which `π` is moreover of finite presentation, keeping `X`, `V` and `φ`.  This
file proves that reduction.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isFinitePresentation_of_exists_epi_idealDirectImage`: from a
  situation of Stacks 0GUY with a surjection `ℰ ↠ π_*ℐ` from a finite locally free module, a
  situation of Stacks 0GUY over the same `X` with `π` finite and of finite presentation and a
  surjection from the same `ℰ`.

## Proof

Write `Y = lim Y_k` with `π_k : Y_k ⟶ X` finite and of finite presentation along closed
immersions, with `π_*𝒪_Y = colim π_{k,*}𝒪_{Y_k}` (Stacks 07VR, in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_affineOver_limit_pushforwardColimit_of_isFinite`).

1. *The module half.*  The composite `ℰ ↠ π_*ℐ ⊆ π_*𝒪_Y` comes from a map
   `φ₀ : ℰ ⟶ π_{k₀,*}𝒪_{Y_{k₀}}` at some stage, since `ℰ` is of finite presentation (Stacks
   07U7).  Let `𝒥 ⊆ 𝒪_{Y_{k₀}}` be the ideal generated by the image of `φ₀` and `𝒩 = π_{k₀,*}𝒥`.
   The image of `𝒩` in `π_*𝒪_Y` is `π_*ℐ`: it contains the image of `ℰ`, and it lies in the ideal
   `π_*ℐ` because the maps of direct-image algebras are multiplicative
   (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.imageSubmodule_pushforwardSubmodule_submoduleIdeal_le`).  The images
   `Ψ_k` of `𝒩` in `π_{k,*}𝒪_{Y_k}` are the direct images of quasi-coherent ideals `ℐ_k` (the
   transition maps are locally surjective,
   `Space.exists_ideal_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_image_pushforwardAlgebraChartMap`),
   they have colimit `π_*ℐ` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_imageSystem_isColimit`), and the
   cokernels of `ℰ ⟶ Ψ_k` are of finite type with epimorphic transition maps and zero colimit,
   so one of them vanishes (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isZero_of_isColimit_of_epi_of_isZero`):
   `ℰ ↠ π_{k,*}ℐ_k` for all large `k`.  This avoids the source's closed subspaces `Z_k`.
2. *The geometric half.*  Since `π_*ℐ` is the image of `π_{l,*}ℐ_l`, the zero locus `V(ℐ)` is
   `V(ℐ_l) ×_{Y_l} Y`
   (`exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_imageSubmodule`),
   so `V` is the open complement of `V(ℐ_l)` in `Y`, and for some `k ≥ l` the open complement of
   `V(ℐ_l) ×_{Y_l} Y_k = V(ℐ_k)` in `Y_k` is `V` itself, through `j ≫ (Y ⟶ Y_k)` (Stacks 07SQ,
   07SL, 07SN, in the form
   `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_iso_openComplement_preimage_of_range_eq_compl_of_mono`).

## Implementation notes

The system of Stacks 07VR lives over the space `⟨X.1, X.2⟩`, which is `X` only up to structure
eta.  Unifying the two inside large terms is very expensive, so every lemma applied to the
system is given `X := ⟨X.1, X.2⟩` explicitly, the new situation is built over `⟨X.1, X.2⟩`, and it
is moved to `X` once, at the top level.  For the same reason the arguments about the chart
modules of the system are stated for an arbitrary cocone of spaces affine over `X`.

All declarations except the main result are private helpers.  Nothing here is registered: the
result is one step of the proof of Stacks 0GV1.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GV1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GV1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GUY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GUY)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07VR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07VR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07U7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07U7)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Stacks.SheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.ImageSubsheaf

universe u

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

/-! ### Images of sheaves of modules -/

section ImageSubmodule

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{u}}
  {M N L : SheafOfModules.{u} R}

/-- If the image of `f ≫ g` lies in `P`, so does the image under `g` of the image of `f`:
membership in `P` is local, and the image of `f` lies locally in the range of `f`. -/
private theorem imageSubmodule_ι_comp_le (f : M ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ L) {P : L.Submodule}
    (h : ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (f ≫ g) ≤ P) :
    ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f).ι ≫ g) ≤ P := by
  refine imageSubmodule_le _ fun X s => ?_
  refine P.isSheaf (((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f).ι ≫ g).val.app X s)
    (J.superset_covering ?_ s.2)
  intro V a ha
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := ha
  have h2 := h _ (apply_mem_imageSubmodule (f ≫ g) m)
  have h3 : (f ≫ g).val.app (op V) m = L.val.map a.op (g.val.app X s.1) := by
    change g.val.app (op V) (f.val.app (op V) m) = _
    rw [hm]
    exact PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply g.val a.op s.1
  rw [h3] at h2
  exact h2

/-- A section of a submodule `ℳ` is carried into `P` by `g` once the image of `ℳ` under `g` is. -/
private theorem mem_of_imageSubmodule_ι_comp_le {M : N.Submodule} {g : N ⟶ L} {P : L.Submodule}
    (h : ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (M.ι ≫ g) ≤ P) {X : Cᵒᵖ} {m : N.val.obj X}
    (hm : m ∈ M.obj X) : g.val.app X m ∈ P.obj X :=
  h X (apply_mem_imageSubmodule (M.ι ≫ g) (⟨m, hm⟩ : M.toSheafOfModules.val.obj X))

/-- The image under `g` of the image of `f` is the image of `f ≫ g`. -/
private theorem imageSubmodule_ι_comp (f : M ⟶ N) (g : N ⟶ L) :
    ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f).ι ≫ g) =
      ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (f ≫ g) := by
  refine le_antisymm (imageSubmodule_ι_comp_le f g le_rfl) (imageSubmodule_le _ fun X m => ?_)
  have h := apply_mem_imageSubmodule ((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f).ι ≫ g)
    ((toImage f).val.app X m)
  have h' : ((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f).ι ≫ g).val.app X ((toImage f).val.app X m) =
      (f ≫ g).val.app X m := by
    change g.val.app X ((toImage f).val.app X m).1 = g.val.app X (f.val.app X m)
    rw [toImage_app_coe]
  rw [h'] at h
  exact h

/-- The image of `f` is contained in the image of `ιN ≫ t` when `f` factors as
`ψ ≫ ιN ≫ t`, the factorization given in two steps. -/
private theorem imageSubmodule_le_of_comp_eq {A N' B' : SheafOfModules.{u} R} (ψ : M ⟶ N')
    (ιN : N' ⟶ A) (t : A ⟶ B') {φ₀ : M ⟶ A} (hψ : ψ ≫ ιN = φ₀) {f : M ⟶ B'}
    (hf : φ₀ ≫ t = f) :
    ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f ≤ ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (ιN ≫ t) := by
  subst hψ hf
  exact ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule_le _ fun X m =>
    apply_mem_imageSubmodule (ιN ≫ t) (ψ.val.app X m)

/-- The image of a submodule which is itself an image, transported along a factorization. -/
private theorem imageSubmodule_ι_comp_eq_of_eq {A : SheafOfModules.{u} R} {P : N.Submodule}
    {f : A ⟶ N} (hP : P = ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule f) {g : N ⟶ L} {h : A ⟶ L}
    (hfg : f ≫ g = h) :
    ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (P.ι ≫ g) = ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule h := by
  subst hP hfg
  exact imageSubmodule_ι_comp f g

/-- A submodule `P` is the image of any epimorphism onto it followed by its inclusion. -/
private theorem le_imageSubmodule_comp_ι [Abelian (SheafOfModules.{u} R)] {P : N.Submodule}
    (e : M ⟶ P.toSheafOfModules) [Epi e] : P ≤ ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (e ≫ P.ι) := by
  intro X s hs
  have hl := isLocallySurjective_of_epi e
  refine J.superset_covering ?_ (hl.imageSieve_mem (⟨s, hs⟩ : P.toSheafOfModules.val.obj X))
  intro V a ha
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := ha
  refine ⟨m, ?_⟩
  exact congrArg Subtype.val hm

end ImageSubmodule

/-! ### Lifting in abelian categories -/

section Abelian

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] [Abelian C]

omit [Abelian C] in
/-- Reassociation with a commuting triangle on the right. -/
private theorem assoc_comp_eq {A₁ A₂ A₃ A₄ : C} (a : A₁ ⟶ A₂) {b : A₂ ⟶ A₃} {c : A₃ ⟶ A₄}
    {d : A₂ ⟶ A₄} (h : b ≫ c = d) : (a ≫ b) ≫ c = a ≫ d := by
  rw [Category.assoc, h]

/-- A property of a composite `j ≫ x ≫ p`, from the property of `j ≫ π` and `x ≫ p = π`. -/
private theorem prop_comp_of_comp_eq {C : Type*} [Category C] (P : ∀ {A B : C}, (A ⟶ B) → Prop)
    {A F G H : C} (j : A ⟶ F) (x : F ⟶ G) (p : G ⟶ H) {π : F ⟶ H} (hx : x ≫ p = π)
    {φ : A ⟶ H} (hj : j ≫ π = φ) (h : P φ) : P (j ≫ x ≫ p) := by
  subst hx hj
  exact h

/-- The composite `(j ≫ x) ≫ p` is `φ` when `x ≫ p = π` and `j ≫ π = φ`. -/
private theorem comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq {C : Type*} [Category C] {A F G H : C} (j : A ⟶ F)
    (x : F ⟶ G) (p : G ⟶ H) {π : F ⟶ H} (hx : x ≫ p = π) {φ : A ⟶ H} (hj : j ≫ π = φ) :
    (j ≫ x) ≫ p = φ := by
  rw [Category.assoc, hx, hj]

/-- Two epi-mono factorizations of one morphism: the first quotient maps onto the second by an
epimorphism compatible with the quotient maps. -/
private theorem exists_epi_comp_eq_of_fac {N Ψ W T : C} (a : N ⟶ Ψ) [Epi a] (b : Ψ ⟶ T)
    [Mono b] (a' : N ⟶ W) [Epi a'] (b' : W ⟶ T) [Mono b'] (h : a ≫ b = a' ≫ b') :
    ∃ l : Ψ ⟶ W, Epi l ∧ a ≫ l = a' := by
  have := StrongEpiCategory.strongEpi_of_epi a
  have sq : CommSq a' a b' b := ⟨h.symm⟩
  refine ⟨sq.lift, ?_, sq.fac_left⟩
  have : Epi (a ≫ sq.lift) := by rw [sq.fac_left]; infer_instance
  exact epi_of_epi a sq.lift

/-- Let `x ≫ m` be an epimorphism `p` onto a subobject `i`, with `m` a monomorphism whose image
`e ≫ m` (for an epimorphism `e`) lies in that subobject.  Then `x` is an epimorphism. -/
private theorem epi_of_comp_mono_eq {E N D T P : C} (x : E ⟶ D) (e : N ⟶ D) [Epi e]
    (m : D ⟶ T) [Mono m] (p : E ⟶ P) [Epi p] (i : P ⟶ T) [Mono i] (r : N ⟶ P)
    (h1 : x ≫ m = p ≫ i) (h2 : e ≫ m = r ≫ i) : Epi x := by
  have := StrongEpiCategory.strongEpi_of_epi p
  have sq : CommSq x p m i := ⟨h1⟩
  have hl : e = r ≫ sq.lift := by
    rw [← cancel_mono m, h2, Category.assoc, sq.fac_right]
  have : Epi (r ≫ sq.lift) := by rw [← hl]; infer_instance
  have : Epi sq.lift := epi_of_epi r sq.lift
  rw [← sq.fac_left]
  infer_instance

/-- **The cokernels of a map from a constant diagram.**  For a colimit cocone `d` of `Ψ` and a map
`γ : E ⟶ Ψ` from the constant diagram such that each `E ⟶ Ψ_k ⟶ colim Ψ` is an epimorphism, the
cokernels of the `γ_k` form a diagram with zero colimit, under `Ψ`, whose transition maps are
epimorphisms where those of `Ψ` are, and a zero cokernel means `γ_k` is an epimorphism. -/
private theorem exists_cokernelDiagram {K : Type*} [Category K] [HasColimitsOfShape K C]
    {Ψ : K ⥤ C} {d : Cocone Ψ} (hd : IsColimit d) {E : C} (γ : (Functor.const K).obj E ⟶ Ψ)
    (hx : ∀ k, Epi (γ.app k ≫ d.ι.app k)) :
    ∃ (Q : K ⥤ C) (π : Ψ ⟶ Q), (∀ k, Epi (π.app k)) ∧ (∀ k, IsZero (Q.obj k) → Epi (γ.app k)) ∧
      (∀ {k l : K} (f : k ⟶ l), Epi (Ψ.map f) → Epi (Q.map f)) ∧
      ∃ cQ : Cocone Q, Nonempty (IsColimit cQ) ∧ IsZero cQ.pt := by
  have hγ : ∀ {k l : K} (f : k ⟶ l), γ.app k ≫ Ψ.map f = 𝟙 E ≫ γ.app l := fun f => by
    simpa using (γ.naturality f).symm
  let Q : K ⥤ C :=
    { obj := fun k => cokernel (γ.app k)
      map := fun {k l} f => cokernel.map (γ.app k) (γ.app l) (𝟙 E) (Ψ.map f) (hγ f)
      map_id := fun k => by ext; simp
      map_comp := fun f g => by ext; simp }
  let π : Ψ ⟶ Q :=
    { app := fun k => cokernel.π (γ.app k)
      naturality := fun k l f => by simp [Q] }
  have hπ : ∀ k, Epi (π.app k) := fun k => inferInstanceAs (Epi (cokernel.π (γ.app k)))
  refine ⟨Q, π, hπ, fun k hk => ?_, fun {k l} f hf => ?_, colimit.cocone Q,
    ⟨colimit.isColimit Q⟩, ?_⟩
  · exact Abelian.epi_of_cokernel_π_eq_zero _ (hk.eq_of_tgt _ _)
  · have : Epi (π.app k ≫ Q.map f) := by rw [← π.naturality f]; exact epi_comp _ _
    exact epi_of_epi (π.app k) (Q.map f)
  · let dc : Cocone Ψ := { pt := colimit Q, ι := π ≫ (colimit.cocone Q).ι }
    have hι : ∀ k, colimit.ι Q k = 0 := fun k => by
      have hh : hd.desc dc = 0 := by
        have := hx k
        rw [← cancel_epi (γ.app k ≫ d.ι.app k), Category.assoc, hd.fac, comp_zero]
        change γ.app k ≫ cokernel.π (γ.app k) ≫ colimit.ι Q k = 0
        rw [cokernel.condition_assoc, zero_comp]
      have := hπ k
      rw [← cancel_epi (π.app k), comp_zero]
      exact (hd.fac dc k).symm.trans (by rw [hh, comp_zero])
    refine (IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero _).2 (colimit.hom_ext fun k => ?_)
    change colimit.ι Q k ≫ 𝟙 _ = colimit.ι Q k ≫ 0
    rw [hι, zero_comp, zero_comp]

/-- The forward map of an isomorphism is an epimorphism. -/
private theorem epi_hom_of_iso {C : Type*} [Category C] {A B : C} (e : A ≅ B) : Epi e.hom :=
  inferInstance

end Abelian

/-! ### The module half: a surjection at a finite stage -/

section ModuleHalf

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
  {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F}

/-- **The surjection onto `π_*ℐ` comes from a finite stage.**  Let `ℳ = colim Φ_k` be a filtered
colimit of quasi-coherent modules on a quasi-compact algebraic space, `𝒩 ⟶ Φ_{k₀}` a map from a
quasi-coherent module of finite type, and `ℰ ⟶ 𝒩`.  Suppose the composite `ℰ ⟶ ℳ` maps onto a
submodule `𝒫 ⊆ ℳ` containing the image of `𝒩`.  Then for all large `k` the map from `ℰ` to the
image of `𝒩` in `Φ_k` is an epimorphism.

The images `Ψ_k` of `𝒩` in `Φ_k` have colimit the image of `𝒩` in `ℳ`, which is `𝒫`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_imageSystem_isColimit`); the cokernels of `ℰ ⟶ Ψ_k` are of finite
type with epimorphic transition maps and zero colimit, so one of them vanishes
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isZero_of_isColimit_of_epi_of_isZero`). -/
private theorem exists_stage_epi_toImage (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS F) {I : Type u}
    [Preorder I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty I]
    {Φ : I ⥤ Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF} {cΦ : Cocone Φ} (hcΦ : IsColimit cΦ)
    (hΦ : ∀ k, (Φ.obj k).IsQuasicoherentOnSite) (hM : cΦ.pt.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    {E N : Modules.{u, u} B S hS F hF} (hN : N.IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hNft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite N) (k₀ : I) (ψ : E ⟶ N) (ιN : N ⟶ Φ.obj k₀)
    (P : cΦ.pt.Submodule) (p : E ⟶ P.toSheafOfModules) [Epi p] (φ₀ : E ⟶ Φ.obj k₀)
    (hψ : ψ ≫ ιN = φ₀) (hφ₀ : φ₀ ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀ = p ≫ P.ι)
    (h₂ : ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (ιN ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀) ≤ P) :
    ∃ l, k₀ ≤ l ∧ ∀ k (hk : k₀ ≤ k), l ≤ k →
      Epi (ψ ≫ toImage (ιN ≫ Φ.map (homOfLE hk))) := by
  have hc' : IsColimit (cΦ.whisker (Under.forget k₀)) :=
    (Functor.Final.isColimitWhiskerEquiv (Under.forget k₀) cΦ).symm hcΦ
  let β : (Functor.const (Under k₀)).obj N ⟶ Under.forget k₀ ⋙ Φ :=
    { app := fun u => ιN ≫ Φ.map u.hom
      naturality := fun u v f => by
        change 𝟙 N ≫ ιN ≫ Φ.map v.hom = (ιN ≫ Φ.map u.hom) ≫ Φ.map f.right
        rw [Category.id_comp, Category.assoc, ← Φ.map_comp, Under.w f] }
  obtain ⟨Ψ, α, eΨ, d, m, e, hα, heΨ, hβ, hΨepi, -, hm, he, hem, -, hed, -, ⟨hd⟩⟩ :=
    exists_imageSystem_isColimit hc' (fun u => hΦ _) hM hN β
  let u₀ : Under k₀ := Under.mk (𝟙 k₀)
  have hem₀ : e ≫ m = ιN ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀ := by
    refine (hem u₀).trans ?_
    change (ιN ≫ Φ.map (𝟙 k₀)) ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀ = ιN ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀
    rw [Φ.map_id, Category.comp_id]
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (exists_factorThru_iff_imageSubmodule_le _).2 h₂
  have hx : Epi (ψ ≫ e) := by
    have := he
    have := hm
    exact epi_of_comp_mono_eq (ψ ≫ e) e m p P.ι r
      (by rw [Category.assoc, hem₀, reassoc_of% hψ, hφ₀]) (hem₀.trans hr.symm)
  let γ : (Functor.const (Under k₀)).obj E ⟶ Ψ := (Functor.const (Under k₀)).map ψ ≫ eΨ
  have hγ : ∀ u, γ.app u = ψ ≫ eΨ.app u := fun u => rfl
  obtain ⟨Q, π, hπ, hQz, hQepi, cQ, ⟨hcQ⟩, hcQz⟩ :=
    exists_cokernelDiagram hd γ fun u => by rw [hγ, Category.assoc, hed]; exact hx
  have hft : (Q.obj u₀).IsFiniteType := by
    have := heΨ u₀
    have := hπ u₀
    exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite _
      (isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS F hF (eΨ.app u₀ ≫ π.app u₀) hNft)
  obtain ⟨u₁, hu₁⟩ := exists_isZero_of_isColimit_of_epi_of_isZero hqc hcQ
    (fun f => hQepi f (hΨepi f)) hcQz hft
  have hγ₁ := hQz u₁ hu₁
  refine ⟨u₁.right, leOfHom u₁.hom, fun k hk hlk => ?_⟩
  let u : Under k₀ := Under.mk (homOfLE hk)
  let f : u₁ ⟶ u := Under.homMk (homOfLE hlk) (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  have hγu : Epi (γ.app u) := by
    have := hΨepi f
    rw [show γ.app u = γ.app u₁ ≫ Ψ.map f by simpa using γ.naturality f]
    exact epi_comp _ _
  have := heΨ u
  have := hα u
  obtain ⟨l, hl, hl'⟩ := exists_epi_comp_eq_of_fac (eΨ.app u) (α.app u) (toImage (β.app u))
    (ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (β.app u)).ι ((hβ u).trans (toImage_ι _).symm)
  change Epi (ψ ≫ toImage (β.app u))
  rw [← hl', ← Category.assoc, ← hγ]
  exact epi_comp _ _

end ModuleHalf



/-! ### The legs of the chart cocone -/

section ChartCocone

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}

/-- The legs of the cocone of chart modules are multiplicative on sections. -/
private theorem chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app_val_app_mul {K : Type*} [Category K]
    {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} (c : Cocone D) (k : K) (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (a b : chartSectionsRing B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left
      ((smallBaseChange B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)).obj Q)) :
    ((chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k).val.app (op Q) (a * b) =
      @HMul.hMul (chartSectionsRing B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left ((smallBaseChange B S hS
          c.pt.unop.obj.hom (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
            c.pt.unop.property)).obj Q))
        (chartSectionsRing B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left ((smallBaseChange B S hS
          c.pt.unop.obj.hom (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
            c.pt.unop.property)).obj Q))
        (chartSectionsRing B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left ((smallBaseChange B S hS
          c.pt.unop.obj.hom (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
            c.pt.unop.property)).obj Q)) instHMul
        (((chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k).val.app (op Q) a)
        (((chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k).val.app (op Q) b) := by
  rw [chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app]
  exact pushforwardAlgebraChartMap_val_app_mul B S hS _ _ _ Q a b

/-- Local surjectivity of a direct-image algebra map, from the quasi-coherent spelling of the
functor of Stacks 081V to the plain one. -/
private theorem isLocallySurjective_affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor_map
    {Z₁ Z₂ : (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} (x : Z₁ ⟶ Z₂)
    (h : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
      ((quasicoherentPushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map x).hom.right.hom) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
      ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map x).right.hom :=
  h

/-- **Stacks 0GV1, the ideals `ℐ_k` of the stages.**  Along a map `k ⟶ l` of a diagram of spaces
affine over `X` whose direct-image algebra map is locally surjective, the image of the direct
image of an ideal `𝒥 ⊆ 𝒪_{Y_k}` in the chart module of `Y_l` is the direct image of a
quasi-coherent ideal `ℐ_l ⊆ 𝒪_{Y_l}`, of finite type when the image is. -/
private theorem exists_ideal_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_image_chartStructureModuleDiagram_map
    {K : Type*} [Category K] {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} {k l : K} (f : k ⟶ l)
    (hα : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (SmallEtale.topology B S hS X.1)
      ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map (D.map f)).right.hom)
    (J : (SheafOfModules.unit (smallEtaleRingSheaf B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left.1
      (D.obj k).unop.obj.left.2)).Submodule)
    (hM : (ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property) _ J).ι ≫
        (chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f)).toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    ∃ I : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.left)).Submodule,
      I.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite ∧
      (SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
          ((ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
            (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property) _ J).ι ≫
              (chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f)).toSheafOfModules :
            Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) →
        SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
          (I.toSheafOfModules : Modules.{u, u} B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.obj.left.2)) ∧
      pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.hom
          (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.property) _ I =
        ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
          (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property) _ J).ι ≫
            (chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f) := by
  rw [chartStructureModuleDiagram_map] at hM ⊢
  exact exists_ideal_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_image_pushforwardAlgebraChartMap B S hS
    (Z₁ := (D.obj l).unop.obj) (Z₂ := (D.obj k).unop.obj)
    (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.property)
    (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)
    (D.obj l).unop.property ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map (D.map f)) hα J hM

/-- **A map of chart modules equal to the direct-image map of a morphism over `X` is pullback of
functions** along any morphism of base-changed charts over that morphism: the hypothesis `ht` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.preimage_eq_of_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_imageSubmodule`. -/
private theorem val_app_eq_appTop_of_eq_pushforwardAlgebraChartMap
    {Z₁ Z₂ : AffineOver B S hS X} (f : Z₁ ⟶ Z₂)
    (t : chartBaseChangeStructureModule B S hS Z₂.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property) ⟶
      chartBaseChangeStructureModule B S hS Z₁.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₁.property))
    (ht : t = pushforwardAlgebraChartMap B S hS
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₁.property)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property)
      ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map f.op))
    (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1)
    (cc : (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₁.property).pullback Q.1.hom ⟶
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property).pullback Q.1.hom)
    (hsnd : cc ≫ (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property).snd Q.1.hom =
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₁.property).snd Q.1.hom)
    (hfst : yoneda.map cc ≫
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property).fst Q.1.hom =
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₁.property).fst Q.1.hom ≫
        f.hom.left.hom)
    (a : chartSectionsRing B S hS Z₂.obj.left
      ((smallBaseChange B S hS Z₂.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ Z₂.property)).obj Q)) :
    t.val.app (op Q) a = ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map cc).appTop.hom a := by
  subst ht
  rw [affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor_map]
  exact pushforwardAlgebraChartMap_pushforwardAlgebraMap_val_app_eq_appTop B S hS
    f.hom _ _ Q cc hsnd hfst a

/-- The legs of the chart cocone are the direct-image maps of the legs, with the leg read as a
morphism out of the cocone point. -/
private theorem chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app_eq {K : Type*} [Category K]
    {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} (c : Cocone D) (k : K) :
    (chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k = pushforwardAlgebraChartMap B S hS
      (Z₁ := c.pt.unop.obj) (Z₂ := (D.obj k).unop.obj)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ c.pt.unop.property)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)
      ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map
        ((c.ι.app k).unop : c.pt.unop ⟶ (D.obj k).unop).op) :=
  chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app B S hS c k

/-- The maps of the chart diagram are the direct-image maps of the transition morphisms. -/
private theorem chartStructureModuleDiagram_map_eq {K : Type*} [Category K]
    {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} {k l : K} (f : k ⟶ l) :
    (chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f = pushforwardAlgebraChartMap B S hS
      (Z₁ := (D.obj l).unop.obj) (Z₂ := (D.obj k).unop.obj)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.property)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)
      ((affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor B S hS X).map ((D.map f).unop).op) :=
  chartStructureModuleDiagram_map B S hS D f

/-- **Stacks 0GV1, the zero loci along a leg of the chart cocone.**  If the direct image of an
ideal `ℐ` of the cocone point is the image of the direct image of an ideal `ℐ'` of a stage, then
`V(ℐ)` is the inverse image of `V(ℐ')`, both closed subspaces of finite presentation. -/
private theorem exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_chartStructureModuleCocone
    (hX : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) {K : Type*} [Category K]
    {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} (c : Cocone D) (k : K)
    (I : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left)).Submodule)
    (hI : IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentIdeal B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left I)
    (I' : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left)).Submodule)
    (hI' : IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentIdeal B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left I')
    (P : (chartBaseChangeStructureModule B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.hom
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ c.pt.unop.property)).Submodule)
    (hP : P = pushforwardSubmodule B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ c.pt.unop.property) _ I)
    (M : (chartBaseChangeStructureModule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)).Submodule)
    (hM : M = pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property) _ I')
    (h : P = ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (M.ι ≫ (chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k)) :
    ∃ (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS c.pt.unop.obj.left.1)
      (Z' : ClosedSubspaces B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left.1),
      definingIdealSheaf B S hS _ Z = I ∧ definingIdealSheaf B S hS _ Z' = I' ∧
        IsFinitePresentation B S hS Z'.1.ι ∧
        Z'.1.preimage ((c.ι.app k).unop : c.pt.unop ⟶ (D.obj k).unop).hom.left.hom = Z.1 := by
  subst hP hM
  have hlegw := Over.w ((c.ι.app k).unop : c.pt.unop ⟶ (D.obj k).unop).hom
  have htl := val_app_eq_appTop_of_eq_pushforwardAlgebraChartMap
    ((c.ι.app k).unop : c.pt.unop ⟶ (D.obj k).unop)
    ((chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k) (chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app_eq c k)
  obtain ⟨Zc, Z', hZc, hZ', -, hZ'fp, hZcZ'⟩ :=
    exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_imageSubmodule hX _ _ hlegw
      c.pt.unop.property (D.obj k).unop.property
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ c.pt.unop.property)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)
      ((chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS c).ι.app k) htl I hI I' hI' h
  exact ⟨Zc, Z', hZc, hZ', hZ'fp, hZcZ'⟩

/-- **Stacks 0GV1, the zero loci along a transition map of the chart diagram.** -/
private theorem exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_chartStructureModuleDiagram
    (hX : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1) {K : Type*} [Category K]
    {D : K ⥤ (AffineOver B S hS X)ᵒᵖ} {k l : K} (f : k ⟶ l)
    (I : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.left)).Submodule)
    (hI : IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentIdeal B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.left I)
    (I' : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left)).Submodule)
    (hI' : IsFiniteTypeQuasicoherentIdeal B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left I')
    (h : pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.property) _ I =
      ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.hom
        (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property) _ I').ι ≫
          (chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f)) :
    ∃ (Z : ClosedSubspaces B S hS (D.obj l).unop.obj.left.1)
      (Z' : ClosedSubspaces B S hS (D.obj k).unop.obj.left.1),
      definingIdealSheaf B S hS _ Z = I ∧ definingIdealSheaf B S hS _ Z' = I' ∧
        Z'.1.preimage (D.map f).unop.hom.left.hom = Z.1 := by
  have hw := Over.w (D.map f).unop.hom
  have ht := val_app_eq_appTop_of_eq_pushforwardAlgebraChartMap (D.map f).unop
    ((chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f) (chartStructureModuleDiagram_map_eq f)
  obtain ⟨Zc, Z', hZc, hZ', -, -, hZcZ'⟩ :=
    exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_imageSubmodule hX _ _ hw
      (D.obj l).unop.property (D.obj k).unop.property
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj l).unop.property)
      (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (D.obj k).unop.property)
      ((chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS D).map f) ht I hI I' hI' h
  exact ⟨Zc, Z', hZc, hZ', hZcZ'⟩

end ChartCocone

/-- A situation of Stacks 0GUY over the space `⟨X.1, X.2⟩` is one over `X`. -/
private theorem exists_of_exists_eta {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
    {hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})} {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    {hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1} {hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1}
    (sit : ResolutionPropertyDescentSituation B S hS hZ (⟨X.1, X.2⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
      hqc hqs)
    (hfp : IsFinitePresentation B S hS sit.π)
    (h : ∃ (E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite E)
      (p : E ⟶ sit.idealDirectImage B S hS hZ), Epi p) :
    ∃ sit' : ResolutionPropertyDescentSituation B S hS hZ X hqc hqs,
      IsFinitePresentation B S hS sit'.π ∧
      ∃ (E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite E)
        (p : E ⟶ sit'.idealDirectImage B S hS hZ), Epi p :=
  ⟨sit, hfp, h⟩

/-! ### The reduction -/

section Reduction

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (hZ : B.Contains (⊤_ Scheme.{u})) {X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS}
    {hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1}
    {hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS hZ X.1}

/-- **The first paragraph of the proof of Stacks 0GV1: reduction to `π` of finite presentation.**
In the situation of Stacks 0GUY over a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic space `X`, if `π_*ℐ`
is a quotient of a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module, then there is a situation of Stacks 0GUY over
the same `X` whose finite morphism `π' : Y' ⟶ X` is moreover of finite presentation, and in which
`π'_*ℐ'` is again a quotient of a finite locally free `𝒪_X`-module (the same one).

The new situation has the same chart `φ : V ⟶ X`; `Y'` is a stage `Y_k` of the limit
presentation `Y = lim Y_k` of Stacks 07VR and `ℐ'` is the ideal `ℐ_k` whose direct image is the
image of the direct image of the ideal generated by a lift of `ℰ ⟶ π_*𝒪_Y` to a stage. -/
theorem exists_isFinitePresentation_of_exists_epi_idealDirectImage
    (sit : ResolutionPropertyDescentSituation B S hS hZ X hqc hqs)
    (h : ∃ (E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite E)
      (p : E ⟶ sit.idealDirectImage B S hS hZ), Epi p) :
    ∃ sit' : ResolutionPropertyDescentSituation B S hS hZ X hqc hqs,
      IsFinitePresentation B S hS sit'.π ∧
      ∃ (E : Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) (_ : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite E)
        (p : E ⟶ sit'.idealDirectImage B S hS hZ), Epi p := by
  obtain ⟨E, hE, p, hp⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨I, _, _, _, DA, ι, -, ⟨hlimP⟩, hfin, -, hclt, ⟨hcolA⟩, hsurj⟩ :=
    exists_affineOver_limit_pushforwardColimit_of_isFinite B S hS sit.π sit.Y.2 X.2
      sit.isFinite_π hqc hqs
  -- the stages `π_k : Y_k ⟶ X`
  have haff : ∀ k : I, IsAffineHom B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom.hom :=
    fun k => (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.property
  have hrep : ∀ k : I, yoneda.relativelyRepresentable (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom.hom :=
    fun k => relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (haff k)
  -- the chart modules `π_{k,*} 𝒪_{Y_k}` and their colimit `π_* 𝒪_Y`
  obtain ⟨hcΦ⟩ := nonempty_isColimit_chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS
    (D := DA.rightOp) (c := coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)) hcolA
  set Φ := chartStructureModuleDiagram B S hS DA.rightOp
  set cΦ := chartStructureModuleCocone B S hS (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι))
  have hΦqc : ∀ k, (Φ.obj k).IsQuasicoherentOnSite := fun k =>
    isQuasicoherentOnSite_smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom
      (hfin (op k)).1 _ (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_unit _)
  have hMqc : cΦ.pt.IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
    isQuasicoherentOnSite_smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS sit.πHom sit.isFinite_π _
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherentOnSite_unit _)
  -- `π_* ℐ ⊆ π_* 𝒪_Y` and the map `φ : ℰ ⟶ π_* 𝒪_Y` onto it
  let P : cΦ.pt.Submodule := pushforwardSubmodule B S hS
    (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.obj.hom
    (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
      (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.property) _ sit.I
  let eP := pushforwardSubmoduleIso B S hS (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.obj.hom
    (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
      (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.property) _ sit.I
  let p' : E ⟶ P.toSheafOfModules := p ≫ eP.inv
  have : Epi p' := epi_comp' hp (epi_hom_of_iso eP.symm)
  let φ : E ⟶ cΦ.pt := p' ≫ P.ι
  -- Stacks 07U7: `φ` comes from a stage `k₀`
  have hEfpo := SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentationOnSite_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite hE
  have : E.IsFinitePresentation :=
    _root_.SheafOfModules.isFinitePresentation_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite' E hEfpo
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_coyoneda_of_isFinitePresentation B S hS X.1 X.2 hZ hqc hqs
    E I
  obtain ⟨k₀, φ₀, hφ₀⟩ := Types.jointly_surjective_of_isColimit
    (isColimitOfPreserves (coyoneda.obj (op E)) hcΦ) φ
  replace hφ₀ : φ₀ ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀ = φ := hφ₀
  have hEqc : E.IsQuasicoherentOnSite := isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite E hE
  have hEft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite E :=
    SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite E
  -- `𝒥 = (im φ₀) · 𝒪_{Y_{k₀}}` and `𝒩 = π_{k₀,*} 𝒥`
  let Mim := ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule φ₀
  have hMimqc : Mim.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
    isQuasicoherentOnSite_imageSubmodule φ₀ hEqc (hΦqc k₀)
  have hMimft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite Mim.toSheafOfModules :=
    isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X.1 X.2 (toImage φ₀) hEft
  let J := submoduleIdeal B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k₀).unop.obj.hom (hrep k₀) Mim
  have hJqc := isQuasicoherentOnSite_submoduleIdeal B S hS _ (hrep k₀) Mim hMimqc
  have hJft := isFiniteTypeOnSite_submoduleIdeal B S hS _ (hrep k₀) Mim hMimft
  let N := pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k₀).unop.obj.hom (hrep k₀) _ J
  let eN := pushforwardSubmoduleIso B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k₀).unop.obj.hom (hrep k₀) _ J
  have hNqc : N.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
    SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso eN.symm
      (isQuasicoherentOnSite_smallBaseChangeModulePushforward B S hS _ (hfin (op k₀)).1 _ hJqc)
  have hNft : SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite N.toSheafOfModules :=
    @isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X.1 X.2 _ _ eN.inv
      (epi_hom_of_iso eN.symm)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFiniteType _
        ((isFiniteType_iff_smallBaseChangePushforward_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS _
          (hfin (op k₀)).1 _ hJqc).1
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite _ hJft)))
  have hMimN : Mim ≤ N := le_pushforwardSubmodule_submoduleIdeal B S hS _ (hrep k₀) Mim
  let ψ : E ⟶ N.toSheafOfModules :=
    N.factorThru φ₀ fun X m => hMimN X (apply_mem_imageSubmodule φ₀ m)
  have hψ : ψ ≫ N.ι = φ₀ := N.factorThru_ι _ _
  have hφP : ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule φ ≤ P :=
    (exists_factorThru_iff_imageSubmodule_le φ).1 ⟨p', rfl⟩
  have hle := imageSubmodule_ι_comp_le φ₀ (cΦ.ι.app k₀) (P := P) (by rw [hφ₀]; exact hφP)
  have hmul₀ := chartStructureModuleCocone_ι_app_val_app_mul
    (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)) k₀
  have hMc := isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS X.1 X.2 _ hMimqc
  have hM : ∀ (Q : SmallEtale B S hS X.1) (m : (Φ.obj k₀).val.obj (op Q)), m ∈ Mim.obj (op Q) →
      (cΦ.ι.app k₀).val.app (op Q) m ∈ P.obj (op Q) :=
    fun Q m hm => mem_of_imageSubmodule_ι_comp_le hle hm
  have h₂ := imageSubmodule_pushforwardSubmodule_submoduleIdeal_le
    (f := (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.obj.hom)
    (hf := relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _
      (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.property)
    (g := (DA.rightOp.obj k₀).unop.obj.hom)
    (hg := relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (DA.rightOp.obj k₀).unop.property)
    (cΦ.ι.app k₀) Mim sit.I hmul₀ hMc (haff k₀) hM
  -- the module half: `ℰ ⟶ π_{k,*} ℐ_k` is an epimorphism for large `k`
  obtain ⟨l, hk₀l, hstage⟩ :=
    exists_stage_epi_toImage hqc hcΦ hΦqc hMqc hNqc hNft k₀ ψ N.ι P p' φ₀ hψ hφ₀ h₂
  -- Stacks 07VR's transition maps carry `π_{k₀,*} 𝒥` onto direct images of ideals `ℐ_k`
  have hc1 : ∀ k (hk : k₀ ≤ k), ∃ Ik : (SheafOfModules.unit (structureRingSheaf B S hS
      (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.left)).Submodule,
      Ik.toSheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite ∧
      SheafOfModules.IsFiniteTypeOnSite
        (Ik.toSheafOfModules : Modules.{u, u} B S hS _ (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.left.2) ∧
      pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom
          (relativelyRepresentable_of_isAffineHom B S hS _ (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.property) _ Ik =
        ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (N.ι ≫ Φ.map (homOfLE hk)) := by
    intro k hk
    obtain ⟨Ik, hqcI, hftI, hI⟩ :=
      exists_ideal_pushforwardSubmodule_eq_image_chartStructureModuleDiagram_map (D := DA.rightOp)
        (homOfLE hk)
        (isLocallySurjective_affinePushforwardAlgebraFunctor_map (DA.rightOp.map (homOfLE hk))
          (hsurj (homOfLE hk).op)) J
        (isQuasicoherentOnSite_imageSubmodule _ hNqc (hΦqc k))
    exact ⟨Ik, hqcI,
      hftI (@isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_epi B S hS X.1 X.2 _ _ (toImage _) (epi_toImage _) hNft), hI⟩
  choose Ik hIkqc hIkft hIk using hc1
  -- `π_* ℐ` is the image of `π_{k₀,*} 𝒥`, hence of every `π_{k,*} ℐ_k`
  have hPN : P = ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule (N.ι ≫ cΦ.ι.app k₀) :=
    le_antisymm ((le_imageSubmodule_comp_ι p').trans
      (imageSubmodule_le_of_comp_eq ψ N.ι (cΦ.ι.app k₀) hψ hφ₀)) h₂
  have hleg : ∀ k (hk : k₀ ≤ k), P = ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule
      ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom (hrep k) _ (Ik k hk)).ι ≫
        cΦ.ι.app k) := fun k hk =>
    hPN.trans (imageSubmodule_ι_comp_eq_of_eq (hIk k hk)
      (assoc_comp_eq N.ι (cΦ.w (homOfLE hk)))).symm
  have htrans : ∀ k l (hk : k₀ ≤ k) (hl : k₀ ≤ l) (hkl : k ≤ l),
      pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj l).unop.obj.hom (hrep l) _ (Ik l hl) =
        ImageSubsheaf.imageSubmodule
          ((pushforwardSubmodule B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom (hrep k) _ (Ik k hk)).ι ≫
            Φ.map (homOfLE hkl)) := fun k l hk hl hkl =>
    (hIk l hl).trans (imageSubmodule_ι_comp_eq_of_eq (hIk k hk) (assoc_comp_eq N.ι
      ((Φ.map_comp _ _).symm.trans (congrArg Φ.map (Subsingleton.elim _ _))))).symm
  -- the leg `Y ⟶ Y_l`: `V(ℐ) = V(ℐ_l) ×_{Y_l} Y` (Stacks 0GV1, via the zero loci)
  obtain ⟨Zc, Z', hZc, hZ', hZ'fp, hZcZ'⟩ :=
    exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_chartStructureModuleCocone (X := ⟨X.1, X.2⟩) hqc
      (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)) l sit.I sit.isFiniteTypeQuasicoherent_I (Ik l hk₀l)
      ⟨hIkqc l hk₀l, hIkft l hk₀l⟩ P rfl _ rfl (hleg l hk₀l)
  -- the open complement of `V(ℐ_l)` at a large stage `k` is the chart `V` (Stacks 07SQ/07SL/07SN)
  have hpre : Z'.1.preimage (((affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙ Over.forget X.1).mapCone
      (Cone.mk _ ι)).π.app (op l)) = Zc.1 := hZcZ'
  have hzl : idealZeroLocus B S hS (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop.obj.left sit.I =
      (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj sit.V) sit.j))ᶜ := sit.idealZeroLocus_I
  have hjT : Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj sit.V) sit.j) =
      (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (Z'.1.preimage
        (((affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙ Over.forget X.1).mapCone
          (Cone.mk _ ι)).π.app (op l))).toFunctor (Z'.1.preimage
        (((affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙ Over.forget X.1).mapCone
          (Cone.mk _ ι)).π.app (op l))).ι))ᶜ := by
    have h1 : Set.range (pointsMap B S hS (yoneda.obj sit.V) sit.j) =
        (Set.range (pointsMap B S hS Zc.1.toFunctor Zc.1.ι))ᶜ := by
      rw [range_pointsMap_ι_eq_idealZeroLocus B S hS _ Zc, hZc, hzl, compl_compl]
    rw [hpre]
    exact h1
  have hcomp : ∀ k : I, ((affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙ Over.forget X.1).mapCone
      (Cone.mk _ ι)).π.app (op k) ≫ (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom.hom = sit.π := fun k =>
    congrArg (fun g => g.hom) (Over.w (((coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).ι.app k).unop :
      (coconeRightOpOfCone (Cone.mk _ ι)).pt.unop ⟶ (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop).hom)
  have hlfp := (hfin (op l)).2.1
  obtain ⟨k, hlk, e, he, hjk, -, -⟩ :=
    exists_iso_openComplement_preimage_of_range_eq_compl_of_mono
      (DA ⋙ (affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙ Over.forget X.1)) l hZ _ hlimP
      (fun a => (DA.obj a).obj.left.2)
      (fun f => isAffineHom_of_isClosedImmersion B S hS _ (hclt f))
      (fun a => isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_of_isFinitePresentation B S hS hZ
        (DA.obj a).obj.left.2 hqs (hfin a).2)
      (fun f => mono_of_isClosedImmersion B S hS _ (hclt f)) sit.Y.2
      (qcqs_of_isFinitePresentation B S hS hZ (DA.obj (op l)).obj.left.2 X.2 hqc hqs
        (hfin (op l)).2).1
      Z'.1 Z'.2 hZ'fp X.2 _ hlfp sit.j sit.isOpenImmersion_j hjT
      (prop_comp_of_comp_eq (fun f => IsEtale B S hS f) sit.j _ _ (hcomp l) sit.comp_eq
        sit.isEtale_φ)
      (prop_comp_of_comp_eq (fun f => IsSurjective B S hS f) sit.j _ _ (hcomp l) sit.comp_eq
        sit.isSurjective_φ)
  -- the transition `Y_k ⟶ Y_l`: `V(ℐ_k) = V(ℐ_l) ×_{Y_l} Y_k`
  have hk₀k : k₀ ≤ k := hk₀l.trans hlk
  obtain ⟨Zk, Zl, hZk, hZl, hZlk⟩ :=
    exists_closedSubspace_preimage_eq_of_chartStructureModuleDiagram (X := ⟨X.1, X.2⟩) hqc
      (D := DA.rightOp) (homOfLE hlk) (Ik k hk₀k) ⟨hIkqc k hk₀k, hIkft k hk₀k⟩ (Ik l hk₀l)
      ⟨hIkqc l hk₀l, hIkft l hk₀l⟩ (htrans l k hk₀l hk₀k hlk)
  obtain rfl : Zl = Z' := definingIdealSheaf_injective B S hS _ (hZl.trans hZ'.symm)
  have hZT : Zk.1 = Zl.1.preimage ((DA ⋙ (affineOverToOver B S hS ⟨X.1, X.2⟩ ⋙
      Over.forget X.1)).map (homOfLE hlk).op) := hZlk.symm
  have hIV := idealZeroLocus_eq_compl_range_of_iso_openComplement Zk hZT _ e he
  rw [hZk] at hIV
  -- the new situation `(V, Y_k, ℐ_k)` over `X`, with `π_k` finite and of finite presentation
  let sit' : ResolutionPropertyDescentSituation B S hS hZ (⟨X.1, X.2⟩ : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
      hqc hqs :=
    { V := sit.V, isAffine_V := sit.isAffine_V, φ := sit.φ, isSurjective_φ := sit.isSurjective_φ,
      isEtale_φ := sit.isEtale_φ, Y := (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.left, j := _,
      π := (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom.hom, isOpenImmersion_j := hjk,
      isFinite_π := (hfin (op k)).1,
      comp_eq := comp_comp_eq_of_comp_eq sit.j _ _ (hcomp k) sit.comp_eq,
      I := Ik k hk₀k, isFiniteTypeQuasicoherent_I := ⟨hIkqc k hk₀k, hIkft k hk₀k⟩,
      idealZeroLocus_I := hIV }
  refine exists_of_exists_eta sit' (hfin (op k)).2 ⟨E, hE, ?_⟩
  -- the surjection `ℰ ⟶ π_{k,*} ℐ_k`
  have hepi := hstage k hk₀k hlk
  let eI := pushforwardSubmoduleIso B S hS (DA.rightOp.obj k).unop.obj.hom (hrep k) _ (Ik k hk₀k)
  let eq₁ := eqToIso (congrArg SheafOfModules.Submodule.toSheafOfModules (hIk k hk₀k).symm)
  exact ⟨(ψ ≫ toImage (N.ι ≫ Φ.map (homOfLE hk₀k))) ≫ eq₁.hom ≫ eI.hom,
    epi_comp' hepi (epi_comp' (epi_hom_of_iso eq₁) (epi_hom_of_iso eI))⟩

